<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Covarra-Ribetex plans IPO.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Covarra-Ribetex plans IPO.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican suit-maker Covarra-Ribetex plans to place about 13.6 percent of its total capital on the Mexican market in an initial public offering, sources close to the issue said.</p>
<p>&quot;They plan to place 12 million shares during a primary offering and another six million during a secondary offering,&quot; said the source, who wished to remain anonymous.</p>
<p>The issue, to be carried out on July 24, will be worth between 150 and 172 million pesos, he said.</p>
<p>The money would be used to increase capacity at the company's various plants, he added.</p>
<p>Banamex-Accival brokerage is the lead manager of the deal.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9565))</p>
